  "title": "prefs: Don't write the extcap prefs to the main preferences",
  "description": "They've been written to extcap.cfg since 4.4.0, so all supported\nversions use that new file, so even people who switch between versions\nwith the same set of preferences shouldn't need them unless they're\nrunning unsupported versions as well.\n\nNote that the capture.no_extcap preference that completely disables\nthe extcaps is not in the extcap_module, but in the capture_module,\nwhich is a good thing because it has to be read first.",
